Conclusions:

  2C 22 22 seems to be zero by analogy to the ASCII version of these files 
  or could be -10000000000.0000 based on HT*.*
  RA numbers should all be positive
  cannot assume first bit24 is sign bit because in RA first hex is A so first bit is 1  (not truncated IEEE 754)
  cannot assume 9th bit bit 15 is sign bit because frequently 3rd hex is A so bit is 1  (not MBF or ByteValue[1])
 
  cannot be possibly truncated 32 MBF see also https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Binary_Format#32-bit_MBF
  Bit 31...24 (8 bit) 	 => bias = 128
  Bit 23      (1 bit)
  Bit 22...0  (23 bit) 
  xxxxxxxx 	s 	mmmmmmm mmmmmmmm mmmmmmmm   

  cannot be IEEE 754 binary32 aka single precision https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single-precision_floating-point_format

  cannot be MRK II NXP 24 bit  https://stackoverflow.com/questions/26930117/float24-24-bit-floating-point-to-hex 
    ByteValue[0] : mantissa bits m7..m0
    ByteValue[1] : sign bit, mantissa bits m14..m8
    ByteValue[2] : exponent e7..e0 (signed, 2s complement repres.)  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two%27s_complement (bias = 1 ?)
    Actual value is
    f = (-1)^s * ( 2^(-1) + m14 * 2^(-2) + ... m0 * 2^(-16) ) * 2^e */

